      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear what you're saying about the \"nuanced understanding,\" but it feels like when you say those other arguments \"overlook\" things, you're basically saying they're wrong or missing the point. If a group of scientists is basing their view strictly on chromosomal and reproductive biology, isn't it a bit unfair to dismiss that as just \"overlooking\" complexity? Isn't that just a way of saying their view is invalid?",
